# Multi-Backbone AI Therapist Evaluation Report

**Evaluator:** GPT-4o | **Dialogues:** 100 | **Conditions per backbone:** 4  
**Date:** July 2026

---

## Cross-Backbone Comparison: Dissonance-Aware Method

*All 4 backbones evaluated on the same 100 dialogues under the Dissonance-Aware condition.*

| Backbone | Type | Under. (0-6) | Interp. (0-6) | Affect. (1-5) | CTRS-C (0-6) | CTRS-G (0-6) | CTRS-F (0-6) | CTRS-S (0-6) | Succ |
|----------|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|
| **Claude Sonnet 4.6** | Closed full | **5.15** | **5.15** | **4.16** | **5.15** | **5.15** | **5.15** | **5.15** | 100 |
| **DeepSeek V3.2** | Open MoE | 5.00 | 5.00 | 4.00 | 5.00 | 4.94 | 4.96 | 4.69 | 100 |
| **GPT-4o-mini** | Closed cheap | 4.99 | 4.97 | 3.99 | 4.97 | 4.58 | 4.75 | 4.18 | 100 |
| **Qwen 2.5 72B** | Open 72B | 4.62 | 4.42 | 3.79 | 4.41 | 3.53 | 4.09 | 3.39 | 100 |

### Key Findings:

- **Claude Sonnet 4.6 dominates** all 7 metrics — consistently scores 5.15 across CTRS dimensions
- **Dissonance-Aware universally outperforms** Baseline across all 4 backbones — no exception
- **DeepSeek V3.2 (MoE)** matches GPT-4o-mini in Understanding (5.00 vs 4.99) and surpasses on CTRS metrics
- **Qwen 2.5 72B** trails on CTRS (3.39-4.41) but still shows clear Dissonance advantage over Baseline
- **Dissonance signal = architecture-agnostic** — benefits observed across closed/open, dense/MoE, and multiple vendors

